---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE, ATTRIBUTION, LEGAL_UPDATED, formatDate } from "../lib/site.mjs";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of use"
  description="Terms for using the Australian Election Tracker and reusing its open data: CC BY 4.0 for data, MIT for code, no warranty, and how to attribute."
>
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Short version: take the data, use it for anything, credit us, and don't pretend we
      said something we didn't.
    </p>

    <h2 id="acceptance">1. These terms</h2>
    <p>
      By using {SITE.domain} you accept these terms. If you don't accept them, don't use
      the site. They apply alongside the
      <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> and <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a>,
      which form part of them.
    </p>

    <h2 id="service">2. What this is</h2>
    <p>
      A free, independent, public-interest record of announced, endorsed and formally
      nominated candidates for Australian elections, published as web pages and as open
      data. It is provided as-is and may change, move or stop at any time. Nobody is
      promised continuity of service.
    </p>

    <h2 id="licence">3. Licence and reuse</h2>
    <p>You are actively encouraged to reuse this material.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Election data</strong> (everything under <code>/data/</code> and the
        <code>data/</code> directory of the repository) is licensed
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="license">CC BY 4.0</a>.
        Use it commercially or non-commercially, adapt it, redistribute it — provided you
        credit <code>{ATTRIBUTION}</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Code</strong> (site, schemas, tooling) is MIT-licensed. See the
        <a href={SITE.repo}>repository</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Page text</strong> — methodology, explanatory writing and these terms —
        is © {new Date(LEGAL_UPDATED).getFullYear()} {SITE.publisher}, and may be quoted
        with attribution.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Logos and branding</strong> are not covered by the above licences. Please
        don't use them in a way suggesting we endorse you or produced your work.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Third-party material — the news articles, party pages and official publications we
      cite — remains the property of its owners. We link to sources; we do not relicense
      them.
    </p>

    <h2 id="attribution">4. Attributing the data</h2>
    <p>
      Attribution is the whole price. Something like:
    </p>
    <p class="cite mono">
      Australian Election Tracker ({SITE.publisher}), {ATTRIBUTION}, CC BY 4.0.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you publish figures drawn from our coverage counts, please carry the
      <a href="/disclaimer#incomplete">coverage caveat</a> with them. Those numbers
      understate reality in a specific, known way, and reproducing them without that
      context misleads your readers rather than ours.
    </p>

    <h2 id="acceptable-use">5. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Please do not:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Present our data as something it isn't — for example, as an official electoral
        commission record, or as a complete list of candidates.
      </li>
      <li>
        Alter records and continue to attribute them to us as though unmodified. Adapt
        freely, but say that you have.
      </li>
      <li>
        Imply that this project, its publisher, or any person associated with it endorses
        a party, candidate, campaign or product.
      </li>
      <li>
        Attempt to interfere with the site's operation or security.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Bulk downloading is explicitly fine — that is what the
      <a href="/data">JSON and CSV exports</a> are for. Please use those rather than
      scraping the HTML; they are smaller, more stable and easier for you.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contributions">6. Contributions</h2>
    <p>
      If you submit a correction, source or pull request, you confirm you are entitled to
      share it and you agree it may be published under the licences above. Nothing is
      published without verification, and we never publish a submitter's identity or
      contact details.
    </p>

    <h2 id="warranty">7. No warranty, and liability</h2>
    <p>
      The site and data are provided without warranty of any kind. Coverage is
      incomplete, verification is ongoing, and the electoral commission is the
      authoritative source — see the <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a>, which sets out
      these limits in full.
    </p>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any loss or damage arising
      from use of, or reliance on, this site or its data. Nothing here excludes any right
      or guarantee that cannot lawfully be excluded, including under the Australian
      Consumer Law.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">8. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may change. The review date below moves when they do, and every prior
      version is visible in the public <a href={SITE.repo}>commit history</a> — you can
      see exactly what changed and when.
    </p>

    <h2 id="law">9. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of Victoria, Australia, and the courts of
      Victoria have jurisdiction.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">10. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>, or
      <a href={SITE.issues}>open an issue</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="updated muted">Last reviewed {formatDate(LEGAL_UPDATED)}.</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  ul strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .cite {
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--surface-2);
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
  .updated {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
</style>
